# Read by `hackmyagent secure` (0.33.x). A line starting with `#` is a comment;
# every other line is one rule:
#   !CHECK-ID                the check is left off the list of findings but is
#                            still scored, still in the verdict and the exit
#                            code, and named on the report's Suppressed line.
#   path                     the file or directory (no globs) is still read; its
#                            findings leave the score and the exit code, and are
#                            counted by severity on the report's Scope line.
#   path:CHECK-ID # reason   that one check on that one path leaves the score
#                            and the exit code, and its findings are counted by
#                            severity on the report's Scope line; every other
#                            check still runs on the path. The `# reason` is
#                            required on this form.
# Any rule may carry `expires:YYYY-MM-DD`. Write it before the `#` of a reason:
# after the `#` it is read as part of the reason and the rule never expires. The
# rule applies through the named day (UTC); from the next day the line is
# reported as an error and its findings return. A line hackmyagent cannot apply
# is reported as a `.hmaignore:<line>` error and is not applied.

package.json:AIM-001 expires:2026-12-31 # agent-runtime-protection is a library that agents import, not an agent; it runs under the identity of the agent that loads it and has none of its own to declare
